			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1578,
				7
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Normalize dispatcher indentation; update Cargo/tauri build identifiers\n\nRe-indent the extracted GenericNotification/Dispatcher and GenericRequest/Dispatcher files to remove the spurious extra block indentation level that was carried over from their original inline positions in CocoonService/mod.rs. Reorder imports (std before third-party) and collapse import brace formatting. No logic changes in either dispatcher.\n\nUpdate Cargo.toml binary/lib/package names and tauri.conf.json identifier/productName to the verbose build configuration string for the development/debug Electron profile, distinguishing this build artifact from production Mountain releases. Preserve originals as .Backup copies.\n\nOutcome: dispatcher code now matches project style conventions, and the development build artifact is correctly labelled for toolchain identification.",
			"SHA": "e78bf315d71ba4a49c4200d7f7002d24f6058255"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T06:13:01Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1576,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract CocoonService dispatchers; fix Send-ness in InitData; retry AppDataPrefix\n\nThe 1400+ line `process_mountain_request` and 600+ line `send_mountain_notification` handlers were inlined in `CocoonService/mod.rs`, making the file unwieldy and obscuring the gRPC service boundary. Extract both match blocks into dedicated `GenericRequest::Dispatcher` and `GenericNotification::Dispatcher` modules, reducing `mod.rs` by ~1900 lines.\n\nIn `InitializationData.rs`, the `MutexGuard` on `WorkspaceFolders` was held across an `.await` call, making the future non-`Send` and breaking `tauri::async_runtime::spawn`. Scope the guard to a block so it is dropped before any await point; extract logging scalars before moving `FoldersWire` into `WorkspaceDTO`.\n\nIn `AppDataPrefix.rs`, replace the `OnceLock<Option<String>>` that caches `None` forever (routing all dev logs to `/tmp` after the first failed resolution) with a two-phase system: `RESOLVED: OnceLock<String>` for the permanent prefix, and `RETRY: Mutex<bool>` that stays `true` on first failure so subsequent writes retry after Tauri has created the app-data directory.\n\nIn `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`, the previous boot-latency fix used a bare `return Ok(...)` inside a match arm, which exits the enclosing async block (not just the arm), changing the block's inferred return type from `()` to `Result<Value, _>` and breaking `Scheduler::Submit`'s `Output = ()` bound. Replace with an `if/else` expression that evaluates to `Ok(...)` in both branches.\n\nAlso fix a minor clippy-nit in `AliasPath.rs` by removing the redundant `.as_str()` call.",
			"SHA": "47a603158ca0d368b2ae744ef8fd7edcf5ed7410"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-20T05:37:16Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1574,
				4
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Reflow long lines and brace placement across four files\n\nNormalize formatting in `UpdateValue.rs`, `WindServiceHandlers/mod.rs`, `InitializationData.rs`, and `CocoonService/mod.rs` to align with Rust style conventions. Changes are limited to comment reflow, static declaration compaction, method body compression, and brace positioning — no logic is altered.\n\nCleans up artifacts from prior commits where formatter passes were missed, keeping the codebase consistent.",
			"SHA": "65f1cf26cfa85fc1639f84d0458df61276bfa44a"
		}
